switch only ever wrote the target tree and never removed anything, so a path
tracked on the source branch but absent from the target survived in the
worktree, read back as an untracked addition, and was committed onto the
target by the next switch's auto-save. workspace.checkout now deletes paths
present in the source tree and absent from the target, then prunes emptied
directories; deletion is driven off the source tree, never a worktree scan,
so untracked and ignored files are never touched. merge.abort and revert
shared the defect and now go through the same path.

openWork returned the process CWD while tracked paths are stored
root-relative, so a checkout run from a subdirectory materialized the whole
repo tree inside it. It now walks up to the directory holding .sdt/.gr,
which fixes every command built on that handle.

revspec.parse rejected any spec without a leading @, and the @ form's hex
selector only scanned moments, so no form resolved the ids sdt log prints.
Hex specs now resolve against the change graph as well as moments, bare or
sigilled, at any unambiguous prefix from 4 to 64; an ambiguous prefix names
